# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.{web,ingestion,migrate} (context = repo root).
#
# Without this file the context carried the whole host `node_modules` (~1 GB of
# platform-specific binaries) into every build, and a `COPY packages ./packages`
# would drop the host's own node_modules/dist on top of the ones pnpm installed
# inside the image.

# Dependency trees: installed inside the image, never copied in.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs. The workspace packages are consumed as TypeScript source
# (every package.json points `exports` at ./src/*.ts and the web app lists them
# in `transpilePackages`), so a stale `dist/` is at best dead weight.
.next
**/.next
**/.next-peer
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and tooling artifacts.
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/playwright/.cache

# Secrets and local state: `.env` is injected at run time via env_file, and the
# federation keypair lives in a named volume. Neither belongs in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docker/volumes

# VCS and editor noise.
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
